  "body": "Direct-PR: record an operator decision on the weekly report format (docs only, no issue: one-session change)\nClaim: cloud/orch\n\n**Problem.** On 2026-11-10 the operator reshaped the weekly report:\n- a morning deck with the overall view (test feedback, fixing the current app, backport into Swift, plus the gap and changelog counts);\n- the KPIs;\n- the progress of M1 to M5;\n- one feature-card slide per milestone;\n- the app day to day;\n- M5;\n- today's decisions.\n\nThe only description of the weekly report was the 6-slide `weekly/build.py` deck.\n\n**Change.** `tooling/roadmap/README.md` gets a \"Weekly report: format\" section with:\n- the slide order;\n- the design language: Apple-style feature cards with a touch of iOS 26/27, and \"the current app\" instead of \"legacy\";\n- the counting rules: a query behind every number, and a credit label is not test feedback.\n\nThe `weekly/build.py` row now points to it. Docs only: no `App/` or `Packages/` file, no macOS job, no ledger entry.\n\n**Tests.** None. Docs consistency and markdownlint run in CI.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CGTbJ8LjeZ6VYEWrtJ)_",
